# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every system. Git for Windows' installer
# sets core.autocrlf, which checks text out with CRLF instead. Git Bash runs a script with CRLF, but
# Linux does not, and a Windows checkout is also used from Linux (WSL, or a container the checkout
# is shared with): there the scripts in tools/, .githooks/ and docker/ stop at their first line ("set:
# Illegal option -"). Rust, Cargo, NSIS and the editors Windows has read LF; this file overrides
# core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, whatever their bytes look like.
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.wasm binary
